11
00:48:42,857 --> 00:48:48,857
Pitch Perfect 3 is a 2017 American musical comedy film directed by
Trish Sie and written by Kay Cannon and Mike White.

12
00:53:08,571 --> 00:53:14,571
It is the sequel to Pitch Perfect 2 (2015), and the
final film in the Pitch Perfect trilogy.

13
00:57:34,285 --> 00:57:40,285
The film features Anna Kendrick, Rebel Wilson, Hailee Steinfeld, Brittany Snow, Anna Camp, Hana Mae Lee, Ester Dean, Chrissie Fit, Alexis Knapp, Kelly Jakle, Shelley Regner,
John Michael Higgins, and Elizabeth Banks—all reprising their roles from previous films—as well as John Lithgow, DJ Khaled, Ruby Rose, Matt Lanter, and Guy Burnet.

14
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:06,000
The plot follows the a capella group the Bellas, who have graduated from college and
are reuniting for one final performance together as part of a USO tour.

15
01:06:25,714 --> 01:06:31,714
Principal photography for Pitch Perfect 3 began in January
2017 in Atlanta, Georgia, and ended that April.

16
01:10:51,428 --> 01:10:57,428
The film was released in the United States on December 22, 2017, and received mixed
reviews from critics, who deemed it inferior to its predecessors.

17
01:15:17,142 --> 01:15:23,142
Nevertheless, it grossed $185 million worldwide against its $45 million budget.

18
01:19:42,857 --> 01:19:48,857
It became the second-highest grossing musical comedy
film of all time, behind Pitch Perfect 2.

19
01:24:08,571 --> 01:24:14,571
The film explores themes of sequel, singer, acapella, uso.

20
01:28:34,285 --> 01:28:40,285
The tone is lighthearted.
